          %h2#Idea Idea
          %h3#broad_idea Broad idea
          %p
            The
            %em Green-Schwarz action functional
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            that describes the propagation of a fundamental super
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+spacetime"} super spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 0
                this is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong
                    Green-Schwarz
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superparticle"} superparticle
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 1
                this is the
                %strong
                  Green-Schwarz
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
                (
                %a{:href => "#GreenSchwarz84"}> Green-Schwarz 84
                )
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p =2
                this is the
                %strong
                  Green-Schwarz
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermembrane"} supermembrane
                (
                %a{:href => "#BergshoeffSezginTownsend87"}> Bergshoeff-Sezgin-Townsend 87
                )
          %p
            The Green-Schwarz model of the superstring is in contrast to the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NSR-string"} NSR-string
            model (the original
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+string"} spinning string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            but no manifest spacetime supersymmetry. It is a non-trivial theorem that the spectrum of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NSR-string"} NSR-string
            enjoys spacetime supersymmetry (after
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GSO+projection"} GSO projection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbative
            excitations of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            background. The construction of the Green-Schwarz functional was motivated by the desire to find an equivalent alternative formulation in which spacetime supersymmetry is manifest (see e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Schwarz16"} Schwarz 16, slides 24-25
          %div
            %p
              %strong>
                manifest
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-models"} sigma-models
              \:
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    manifest
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
                    supersymmetry
                  %th manifest target+worldvolume supersymmetry
                  %th
                    manifest
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
                    supersymmetry
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NSR+action+functional"} NSR action functional
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superembedding+approach"} superembedding approach
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            %center
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/pBraneEmbedding.jpg", :width => "800"}/
            %blockquote
              %p
                graphics grabbed from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Super-exceptional+embedding+construction+of+the+M5-brane"} FSS19c
          %p
            For more discussion see also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+fundamental+super+p-branes"} geometry of physics – fundamental super p-branes
          %h3#more_details More details
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} Perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            on geometric backgrounds is defined by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond+model"} Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+super+conformal+field+theories"} 2d super conformal field theories
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+charge"} central charge
            15) on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheets"} worldsheets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            that are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Riemann+surfaces"} super Riemann surfaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spaces"} target spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that are ordinary (i.e. “bosonic”)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
          %p
            These
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theories"} field theories
            are induced from
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functionals"} action functionals
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy+functional"} energy functional
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+action"}> Polyakov action
            ) on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,X]
            of smooth functions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi \;\colon\; \Sigma \longrightarrow X
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            to target
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The central theorem of perturbative superstring theory (the no ghost theorem with
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GSO+projection"} GSO projection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
            are the quanta of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbations
            of a higher dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
            on target spacetime, hence transforms under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            on target spacetime.
          %p This is the fundamental prediction of the assumption of fundamental strings:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                assuming that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+particles"} fundamental particles
                that run in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
                are fundamentally (at high energy) the ground state modes of a fundamental
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
            %li
              %p
                demanding that there are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermionic
                particles among these,
          %p implies
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                that the string must be the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+string"} spinning string
                (have fermions in its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
                theory), which in turn implies…
            %li
              %p
                that it is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
                (worldsheet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
                mixes the worldsheet bosons and fermions), precisely: the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond+superstring"} Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond superstring
            %li
              %p
                that its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
                theory, hence that also the effective target space fields exhibit
                %em local
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
                (i.e. “high energy supersymmetry”, different from “low energy supersymmetry” that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHC"} LHC
                was looking for).
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  main theorem of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative super-string theory
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %munder
                            %mrow
                              %mtext fermions
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mo +
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mtext strings
                            %mo ⏟
                          %mtext spinning string
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtext superstring
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtext supergravity
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\text{spinning string}}{\underbrace{\text{fermions} \;+\; \text{strings}}} \;=\; \text{superstring} \;\Rightarrow\; \text{supergravity}
          %p
            The first step in this implication (identifying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+string"} spinning string
            as the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            was discovered in “the west”, in the first place), but the second step (that the superstring excitations necessarily are quanta of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            theory) appears as a miracle from the point of view of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond+superstring"} Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond superstring
          %p
            In order to improve on this situation,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"} Michael Green
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
            searched for and found (
            %a{:href => "#GreenSchwarz81"}> Green-Schwarz 81
            ,
            %a{:href => "#GreenSchwarz82"} Green-Schwarz 82
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GreenSchwarz84"} Green-Schwarz 84
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Schwarz16"} Schwarz 16, slides 24-25
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            that would manifestly exhibit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
                  for
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
                %th
                  manifest
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz+super-string"} Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz super-string
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Green-Schwarz super-string
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
          %p
            The basic idea is to pass to the evident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometric
            analogue of the bosonic string action:
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed manifold
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            2 – representing the abstract
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            of a string. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+manifold"} pseudo-Riemannian manifold
            – representing a purely
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravitational
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            background. Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            governing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
            propagating in this spacetime is the functional
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mi ℏ
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi bos
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℝ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℏ
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar} S_{bos})
                  \\;\colon\;
                  [\Sigma,X]
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbb{R}/_{\hbar}\mathbb{Z}
          %p
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,X]
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \to X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativity"} relativistic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume"} volume
            of the image of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi kin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %msub
                    %mi vol
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo *
                      %mi g
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Sigma\overset{\phi}{\longrightarrow} X)
                  \\;\mapsto\;
                  S_{kin}(\phi)
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\int_\Sigma vol_{\phi^\ast g}
                  \\,.
          %p
            (This is the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nambu-Goto+action"} Nambu-Goto action
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+action"} Polyakov action
            which is the genuine starting point for the quantum
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz+super-string"} Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz super-string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-branes"} p-branes
            it is more natural to consider the Nambu-Goto form of the action here.)
          %p
            When here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
            is generalized to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspacetime"} superspacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"} orthogonal structure
            encoded by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-vielbein"} super-vielbein
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,X]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superisometry+group"} superisometry group
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mtext symmetry of worldsheet theory
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %mi Σ
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %msup
                                    %mrow
                                    %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                      %mi ϕ
                                  %mo ↙
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %msup
                                    %mo ↘
                                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi ϕ
                                        %mo ′
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mi X
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %munder
                                    %mo ⟶
                                    %mo ≃
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mtext super-isometry of target spacetime
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\text{symmetry of worldsheet theory}
                  \\\
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \Sigma
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\phi}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{\phi'}}
                  \\\
                  X &amp;&amp;\underset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}&amp;&amp; X
                  }
                  \\\
                  \\text{super-isometry of target spacetime}
                  }
          %p
            However,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"} Green
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} Schwarz
            noticed that this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kinetic+action"} kinetic action
            functional
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %msub
                    %mi vol
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo *
                      %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \mapsto \int_\Sigma vol_{\phi^\ast e}
            does
            %em not
            quite yield dynamics that is equivalent to that of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond+super-string"} Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond super-string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            hold (“on
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz+super-string"} Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz super-string
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi WZW
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{WZW}
            (whose notation we explain in a moment) to the plain super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nambu-Goto+action"} Nambu-Goto action
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi kin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{kin}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            enjoys a further 1-parameter
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kappa-symmetry"} kappa-symmetry
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi GS
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi kin
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi WZW
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_{GS} = S_{kin} + S_{WZW}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover, they showed that restricting the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamics"} dynamics
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+superstring"} Green-Schwarz superstring
            to the
            = succeed "-symmetric" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz+super-string"} Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz super-string
          %p
            Finally they showed that when
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixing
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light-cone+gauge"} light-cone gauge
            (which is possible whenever
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target spacetime
            admits two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lightlike"} lightlike
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+vector"} Killing vector
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+string"} Green-Schwarz string
            may be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantized
            by a standard procedure and the resulting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+system"} quantum
            dynamics is equivalent to that of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond+super-string"} Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond super-string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
            for the observed local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            of super-string
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+superstring"} Green-Schwarz superstring
            away from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light+cone+gauge"} light cone gauge
            remains an open problem.)
          %p
            While Green-Schwarz’s extra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kappa-symmetry"} kappa-symmetry
            term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi WZW
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{WZW}
            this serves a clear purpose as a means to an end, originally its geometric meaning was mysterious. However, in (
            %a{:href => "#HenneauxMezincescu85"}> Henneaux-Mezincescu 85
            ) it was observed (expanded on in (
            %a{:href => "#Rabin87"}> Rabin 87
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AzcarragaTownsend89"} Azcarraga-Townsend 89
            = succeed "))," do
              %a{:href => "#AzcarragaIzquierdo95"} Azcarraga-Izquierdo 95,chapter 8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            describing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-string"} super-string
            in
            = succeed "-dimensions" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d+1
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+WZW+model"} parameterized
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wess-Zumino-Witten+model"} Wess-Zumino-Witten model
            for
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
                being locally
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|\mathbf{N}}
                regarded as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset"} coset
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"} supergroup
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi N
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi Iso
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}}
                      \\;\simeq\;
                      Iso(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}}) / Spin(d-1,1)
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{N}
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+spin+representation"} real spin representation
                (the “number of supersymmetries”),
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Iso
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Iso(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}})
                the corresponding
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} super Poincaré group
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d-1,1)
                its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+manifold"} Lorentz-signature
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} Spin
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW-term"} WZW-term
                being a local potential for the unique (up to rescaling, if it exists)
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Spin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d-1,1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} super Lie algebra 3-cocycle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{F1}
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔦𝔰𝔬
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mrow
                            %mi d
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{iso}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}})
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+algebra"} Clifford algebra
                representation; in terms of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vielbein"} super vielbein
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e^a, \psi^\alpha)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mover
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi A
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi e
                        %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mu_{F1} = \overline{\psi} \wedge \Gamma_A \psi \wedge e_a
              %p
                and so in components the bi-fermionic component of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{F1}
                is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mi α
                          %mi β
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mi α
                          %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (\mu_{F1})_{a \alpha \beta} = \Gamma_{a \alpha \beta}
              %p and all other components vanish.
          %p
            More in detail, just as ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1}
            may be identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/translation+group"} translation group
            along itself, with canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+1-forms"} left invariant 1-forms
            given by the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
            field
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo ≔
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi a
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{e^a \coloneqq \mathbf{d}x^a\}_{a = 0}^{d-1}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x^a\}
            are the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}}
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+spin+representation"} real spin representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{N}
            is characterized as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"} supergroup
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+1-forms"} left invariant 1-forms
            constitute the
            = succeed "-bigraded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-vielbein"} super-vielbein
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi a
                      %mo ⏟
                    %mrow
                      %mi deg
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi even
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mover
                    %mi θ
                    %mo ¯
                  %msup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi a
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi θ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi α
                      %mo ⏟
                    %mrow
                      %mi deg
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi odd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi θ
                    %mi α
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{deg = (1,even)}{\underbrace{e^a}}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\mathbf{d}x^a + \overline{\theta}\Gamma^a \mathbf{d} \theta
                  \\;\;\;\,,\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  \\underset{deg = (1,odd)}{\underbrace{\psi^\alpha}} \;\coloneqq\; \mathbf{d}\theta^\alpha
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi θ
                    %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x^a, \theta^\alpha)
            are the canonical coordinates on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi θ
                    %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\theta^\alpha\}
            spanning the given real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+representation"} Spin(d-1,1)-representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{N}
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+algebra"} Clifford algebra
            generators
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\Gamma^a\}
          %p
            Now while ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1}
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left-invariant+1-forms"} left-invariant 1-forms
            are all closed
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi on
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{d}e^a = 0 \;\;\;\;\;\; on \; \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1}
                  \\,,
          %p
            the key phenomenon of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            (that two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
            pair to a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosons"} bosons
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}}
            is slightly non-abelian, reflected by the fact that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-vielbein"} super-vielbein
            is not closed
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mover
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi a
                  %mi ψ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi α
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{d} e^a =  \overline{\psi} \wedge \Gamma^a \psi
                  \\;\,,\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  \\mathbf{d} \psi^\alpha = 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            This elementary effect is the source of all the rich structure seen in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+super-string"} Green-Schwarz super-string
            and generally in all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super p-brane
            theory. (The above differential is equivalently that in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            is the super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            literature this is referred to a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tau+cohomology"}> tau cohomology
            ”.)
          %p
            In particular, for special combinations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            and number of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetries"} supersymmetries
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{N}
            (i.e.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+spin+representation"} real spin representation
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mover
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi a
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mu_{F1} =  \overline{\psi} \wedge \Gamma_a \psi \wedge e^a
          %p
            is a non-trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cocycle"} Lie algebra cocycle
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{d}\mu_{F1} = 0
            and so that there is no
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+differential+form"} left invariant differential form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi b
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{d}b = \mu_{F1}
            (beware here the left-invariance condition: there are of course non-left-invariant potentials for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{F1}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+densities"} Lagrangian densities
            for the WZW action functional
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi WZW
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{WZW}
          %p This happens notably for
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mn 10
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 10
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 16
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{N} = (1,0) = \mathbf{16}
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"}> heterotic string
                )
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mn 10
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 10
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 16
                      %mo +
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 16
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{N} = (2,0) = \mathbf{16} + \mathbf{16}
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIB+superstring"}> type IIB superstring
                )
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mn 10
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 10
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi N
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 16
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 16
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{N} = (1,1) = \mathbf{16} + \mathbf{16}^\ast
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+superstring"}> type IIA superstring
                ).
          %p
            (It also happens in some lower dimensions, where however the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond+string"} Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond string
            develops a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+anomaly"} conformal anomaly
            after
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            (a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-critical+string"}> non-critical string
            ”). This classification of cocycles is part of what has come to be known as the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            in superstring theory, see below.)
          %p
            In this equivalent formulation, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            for the superstring has the following simple form:
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,e)
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspacetime"} superspacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-vielbein"} super-vielbein
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            (super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"}> orthogonal structure
            ) which is locally modeled on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}}
            (technically: a
            = succeed "-free" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+of+a+G-structure"} torsion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Cartan+geometry"} super-Cartan geometry
            modeled on
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Iso
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(d-1,1) \hookrightarrow Iso(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                    %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{F1}^X \in \Omega^3(X)
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+differential+form"} super differential form
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            which is the induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+globalization+of+WZW+term"} definite globalization
            of the cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{F1}
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
            any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+topological+space"} contractible
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                    %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi U
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^X_{F1}|_{U} \in \Omega^3(U)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{F1}^X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is exact, and hence admits a potential
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_U \in \Omega^2(U)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
                    %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mn 1
                      %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{d} B = \mu^X_{F1}|_U
          %p
            Then for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            a 2-dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mi ℏ
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi GS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi U
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℝ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℏ
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar} S_{GS})
                  \\;\colon\;
                  [\Sigma,X]_U
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbb{R}/_{\hbar} \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            is the function on the super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+mapping+space"} smooth mapping space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,X]_U
            of morphisms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifolds"} supermanifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon \Sigma \to X
            which factor through
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %msub
                    %mi vol
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo *
                      %mi e
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo +
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi μ
                    %mn 3
                    %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi U
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi
                  \\;\mapsto\;
                  \\int_\Sigma vol_{\phi^\ast e}
                  \\;+\;
                  \\int_\Sigma \phi^\ast B_U
                  \\;\;\;\,,\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  \\mathbf{d} B_U = \mu^X_3|_U
                  \\,.
          %p
            In order to get rid of the restriction to some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chart"} chart
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subset X
            one needs to add global data. The need for this is at least mentioned briefly in (
            %a{:href => "#Witten86"}> Witten 86, p. 261 (17 of 20)
            ), but seems to have otherwise been ignored in the physics literature. The general solution is to promote the local potentials
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            to the connection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat B
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Super+Gerbes"} super gerbe
            (
            %a{:href => "#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber13"}> FSS 13
            ). This is a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+prequantization"} higher prequantization
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℝ
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi ℏ
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mtext prequantization
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mover
                                %mi B
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi curv
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msubsup
                                %mi μ
                                %mrow
                                  %mi F
                                  %mn 1
                                %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Ω
                            %mn 3
                        %mtd
                          %mtext 3-form curvature
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}^{2}(\mathbb{R}/_\hbar \mathbb{Z}) &amp; \text{prequantization}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\hat B}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{curv}}
                  \\\
                  X
                  \&amp;\underset{\mu^X_{F1}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\mathbf{\Omega}^3
                  \&amp;
                  \\text{3-form curvature}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Writing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo *
                  %mover
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_\Sigma \phi^\ast \hat B
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+holonomy"} volume holonomy
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-bundle+with+connection"} circle 2-bundle with connection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat B
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mi ℏ
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi GS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℝ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℏ
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar} S_{GS})
                  \\;\colon\;
                  [\Sigma, X]
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbb{R}/_\hbar\mathbb{Z}
          %p is given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %msub
                    %mi vol
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo *
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo *
                  %mover
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi curv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                    %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi \;\mapsto\; \int_\Sigma vol_{\phi^\ast} + \int_\Sigma \phi^\ast \hat B
                  \\;\;\,,
                  \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  curv(\hat B) = \mu_{F1}^X
                  \\,.
          %p
            This form of the Green-Schwarz action functional for the string has evident generalization to other
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-branes"} p-branes
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} Spin(d-1,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
            = succeed "-cocycle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p+2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{p+2}
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}}
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+prequantum+line+bundle"} higher prequantum line bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat C
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^X_{p+2}
            and consider the analogous functional.
          %p
            The triples
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi N
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d,\mathbf{N},p)
            (spacetime dimension, number of supersymmetries, dimension of brane) such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi Γ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mi ⋯
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi p
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mu_{p+2}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\overline{\psi} \wedge \Gamma^{a_1 \cdots a_p} \psi \wedge e_{a_1} \wedge \cdots \wedge e_{a_p}
          %p
            is a nontrivial cocycle, hence for which there is such a Green-Schwarz action functional for
            = succeed "-branes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1\vert \mathbf{N}}
            may be classified and form what is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            (
            %a{:href => "#AETW87"}> Achúcarro, Evans, Townsend &amp; Wiltshire 87
            ,
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#Brandt12-13"} Brandt 12-13
          %p#DuffBraneScan
          %div{:style => "float:left;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
            %img{:height => "600", :src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/DuffBraneScan.jpg"}/
          %p
            The graphics on the left is from (
            %a{:href => "#Duff87"}> Duff 87
            ). The diagonal lines indicate
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p+1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d+1)
            dimensions to a
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "-dimensions." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
          %p
            For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 11
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 32
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d = 11, \; \mathbf{N} = \mathbf{32}, \; p = 2)
            one finds a cocycle, and the corresponding GS-action functional is that of the fundamental
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
          %p
            This was a striking confluence of brane physics and classification of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 11
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 11
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mn 5
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 5
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+fields"} higher gauge fields
            on their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            (tensor multiplets).
          %p
            An action functional for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            analogous to a Green-Schwarz action functional was found in (
            %a{:href => "#BLNPST97"}> BLNPST 97
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#APPS97"} APPS 97
          %p
            In order to deal with this, it was suggested in (
            %a{:href => "#CAIB99"}> CAIB 99
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Sakaguchi00"} Sakaguchi 00
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AzcarragaIzquierdo01"} Azcarraga-Izquierdo 01
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super-Minkowski+spacetimes"} extended super-Minkowski spacetimes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            and serves to unify the Green-Schwarz-like models for the D-branes and the M5-brane with the original Green-Schwarz models for the string and the M2-brane.
          %p
            These
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super-Minkowski+spacetimes"} extended super-Minkowski spacetimes
            carry algebraic analogs of super Lie algebra cocycles, such that the relevant terms for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            do appear after all, hence such that all the branes in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            are unified. In fact these “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super-Minkowski+spacetimes"}> extended super-Minkowski spacetimes
            ” are precisely the “FDA”s that have been introduced before in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fr%C3%A9+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fré formulation of supergravity
            and what became identified as the 7-cocycle for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            this way had earlier been recognized algebraically as an stepping stone for an elegant re-derivation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            (
            %a{:href => "#DAuriaFre82"}> D’Auria-Fré 82
            ).
          %p
            The (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"}> higher
            ) geometric meaning of these constructions was found in (
            %a{:href => "#FiorezaSatiSchreiber13"}> Fiorenza-Sati-Schreiber 13
            ): these algebraic structures of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super-Minkowski+spacetimes"}> extended super-Minkowski spacetimes
            ”/FDAs are precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
            of
            = succeed "-extensions" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+n-algebra"} super Lie n-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Minkowski+spacetime"} super-Minkowski spacetime
            which are classified by the cocycles that serve as the GS-WZW terms of the
            = succeed "-branes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1
            = succeed "-branes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_2
          %p
            Hence the missing
            = succeed "-branes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            (classifying just cocycles on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebras"} super Lie algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+homotopy+Lie+algebras"} strong homotopy Lie algebras
            \=
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebras"} L-infinity algebras
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extension
            and so the old brane scan is generalized to a tree of branes
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} The brane bouquet
          %p
            %img{:alt => "the brane bouquet", :src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/BraneBouquetWithDualities.jpg", :width => "900"}/
          %p
            Each item in this bouquet denotes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-infinity+algebra"} super L-infinity algebra
            and each arrow denotes an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+extension"} L-infinity extension
            classified by a cocycle which encodes the GS-WZW term of the brane named by the domain of the arrow. Moreover, arrows pass exactly from one brane species to the brane species that may end on the former.
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber13"}> Fiorenza-Sati-Schreiber 13
            ) it is shown that all these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-infinity+algebras"} super L-infinity algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integrate
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+super-n-groups"} smooth super-n-groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integrate
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Super+Gerbes"} super-gerbes
            on these, such that the induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+holonomy"} volume holonomy
            is the relevant generalized GS-WZW term. For detailed exposition see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Structure+Theory+for+Higher+WZW+Terms"} Structure Theory for Higher WZW Terms
          %p
            With this generalized perspective, now the Green-Schwarz-type action functionals describe
            %em all
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-branes"} p-branes
            in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
          %p
            Again, in order to make this generally true one needs to apply a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+prequantization"} higher prequantization
            – a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+n-bundle+with+connection"} line (p+1)-bundle with connection
            – in order to globalize the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW-terms"} WZW-terms
            (
            %a{:href => "#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber13"}> Fiorenza-Sati-Schreiber 13
            )
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℝ
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi ℏ
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mtext prequantization
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi A
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi p
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi curv
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %msubsup
                                %mi μ
                                %mrow
                                  %mi p
                                  %mo +
                                  %mn 2
                                %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Ω
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo +
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtext -form curvature
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}^{p+1}(\mathbb{R}/_\hbar \mathbb{Z}) &amp; \text{prequantization}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\hat A_{p+1}}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{curv}}
                  \\\
                  X
                  \&amp;\underset{\mu^X_{p+2}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\mathbf{\Omega}^{p+2}
                  \&amp;
                  (p+2)\text{-form curvature}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Hence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A_{p+1}
            is the actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+field"} background field
            that the
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A_p
            than in its curvature
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi curv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} curv(\hat A_{p+1}) = \mu_{p+2}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            one may find the local super
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            for local choices of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A_{p+1}
            for the given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{4}
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactifications"} KK-compactifications
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/body"} body
            of this moduli space is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+tangent+bundle"} exceptional tangent bundle
            on which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-duality"} U-duality
            group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E7"} E7
            has a canonical action (see at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/From+higher+to+exceptional+geometry"} From higher to exceptional geometry
          %p
            This highlights that Green-Schwarz functionals capture fundamental (“microscopic”) aspects of
            = succeed "-branes." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
