                %th
                  \-fluctuations about asymptotic AdS configuration
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo →
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
                %th
                  solitonic
                  = succeed "-brane" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Green-Schwarz action functional
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric"}> super
                  \-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal field theory
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#ClausKalloshProeyen97"}> Claus-Kallosh-Proeyen 97
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ClausKalloshKumarTownsend98"} Claus-Kallosh-Kumar-Townsend 98
            %a{:href => "#AFFFTT98"} AFFFTT 98
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#PastiSorokinTonin99"} Pasti-Sorokin-Tonin 99
          %p
            In fact the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS-state"} BPS-state
            condition itself is neatly encoded in the Green-Schwarz action functionals: by construction they are invariant under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superisometry+group"} superisometry group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noether+theorem"} Noether theorem
            implies that there are corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+currents"} conserved currents
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dickey+bracket"} Dickey bracket
            forms a super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+extension"} Lie algebra extension
            of the Lie algebra of supersymmetries.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
