          %p
            Here the “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⇙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \swArrow
            ” filling the triangles is the non-trivial gauge transformation by which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+term"} WZW term
            (as any WZW term) is preserved under the symmetries (instead of being fixed identically). It is the information in this transformations which makes the currents form an extension of the symmetries.
          %p Here this yields the famous brane charge extensions of the super-isometry super Lie algebra of the schematic form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
