            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
          %p
            Detailed discussion of the above steps is in (
            %a{:href => "#AFFFTT98"}> AFFFTT 98
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#PastiSorokinTonin99"} Pasti-Sorokin-Tonin 99
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superconformal+algebra"} super-conformal
            brane scan” is discussed in
            %a{:href => "#BlencoweDuff88"} Blencowe &amp; Duff 1988
            with further developments in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Duff09"} Duff 2009
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Duff21"} Duff 2021
          %h3#quantization Quantization
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of the Green-Schwarz super
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+models"} sigma models
            is discussed in the literature in terms of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light-cone+gauge+quantization"} light-cone gauge quantization
          %p
            This is actually how the Green-Schwarz superstring was first introduced in (
            %a{:href => "#GreenSchwarz81"}> Green-Schwarz 81
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GreenSchwarz82"} Green-Schwarz 82
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+covariance"} generally covariant
            formulation was found in (
            %a{:href => "#GreenSchwarz84"}> Green-Schwarz 84
            ). A textbook account of this is in (
            %a{:href => "#GreenSchwarzWitten"}> Green-Schwarz-Witten, section 5
            ).
          %p
            While, by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            discussed above, the action functional for the Green-Schwarz superstring exists for target
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} super Minkowski spacetimes
            of dimension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light-cone+gauge+quantization"} light-cone gauge quantization
            produces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomaly"} quantum anomaly
            for the spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz group
            symmetry in dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 4
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 6
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 6
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 10
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 10
            the anomaly disappears and the thus quantized Green-Schwarz string becomes equivalent to the quantum
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NSR+string"} NSR string
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+string+theory"} type II string theory
          %p
            Curiously, the light-cone gauge quantization of the GS-string also does wor however for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 3
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+1-brane+in+3d"} super 1-brane in 3d
            for more on this.
