                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"} Dan Freed
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Kazhdan"}> David Kazhdan
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Morgan"} John Morgan
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantum+Fields+and+Strings"}> Quantum Fields and Strings
                , A course for mathematicians
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/qft"} web version
          %p
            Textbook discussion of the Green-Schwarz version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            is in
          %ul
            %li#CastellaniDAuriaFre91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Castellani"}> Leonardo Castellani
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"} Riccardo D'Auria
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Supergravity+and+Superstrings+-+A+Geometric+Perspective"} Supergravity and Superstrings - A Geometric Perspective
          %p Comprehensive review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joan+Sim%C3%B3n"}> Joan Simón
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Brane Effective Actions, Kappa-Symmetry and Applications
              %strong 15
              3 (2012) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1110.2422"}> arXiv:1110.2422
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.12942/lrr-2012-3"} doi:10.12942/lrr-2012-3
          %p
            Quantization of the Green-Schwarz string using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+spinors"} pure spinors
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+A.+Grassi"}> Pietro A. Grassi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giuseppe+Policastro"} Giuseppe Policastro
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+van+Nieuwenhuizen"} Peter van Nieuwenhuizen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An Introduction to the Covariant Quantization of Superstrings
                %strong 20
                (2003) 395-410 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0302147"}> arXiv:hep-th/0302147
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+A.+Grassi"}> Pietro A. Grassi
                , Y. Oz,
                %em Non-Critical Covariant Superstrings
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0507168"}> arXiv:hep-th/0507168
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Review in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superembedding+approach"} superembedding approach
          %ul
            %li#Sorokin99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Sorokin"}> Dmitri Sorokin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Superbranes and Superembeddings
              %strong 329
              (2000) 1-101 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9906142"}> arXiv:hep-th/9906142
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The observation that the Green-Schwarz action functional is an example of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW-model"} WZW-model
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Minkowski+spacetime"} super-Minkowski spacetime
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#HenneauxMezincescu85
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Henneaux"}> Marc Henneaux
              , Luca Mezincescu,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  A
                  = succeed "-Model" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              %strong 152
              (1985) 340 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(85)90507-6"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(85)90507-6
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/15922"} spire:15922
          %p
            For more references on this WZW perspective see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ReferencesWZWTerm"} below
          %p
            For references on curved backgrounds see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ReferencesSupergravityBackgroundEquationsOfMotion"} below
          %div
            %h3#SuperMembraneAsSigmaModelReferences Super-membrane/M2-brane as a sigma model
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-type" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-model"} Green-Schwarz sigma-model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-membrane"} super-membrane
              in 11d (as in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
              and in contrast to the
              = succeed "-solutions" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11d+supergravity"} 11d supergravity
            %ul
              %li#BergshoeffSezginTownsend87
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Bergshoeff"}> Eric Bergshoeff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supermembranes and eleven-dimensional supergravity
                %strong 189
                (1987) 75-78 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(87)91272-X"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(87)91272-X
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/248230/"} spire:248230
            %p
              Via the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superembedding+approach"} superembedding approach
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
              were obtained in
            %ul
              %li#BPSTV95
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Pasti"} Paolo Pasti
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Sorokin"} Dmitri Sorokin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mario+Tonin"} Mario Tonin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Volkov"} Dmitry Volkov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superstrings and supermembranes in the doubly supersymmetric geometrical approach
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9501113"} arXiv:hep-th/9501113
            %p
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
              in:
            %ul
              %li#HoweSezgin05
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"}> Paul Howe
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The supermembrane revisited
                %strong 22
                (2005) 2167-2200 [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0412245"}> arXiv:hep-th/0412245
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/0264-9381/22/11/017"} doi:10.1088/0264-9381/22/11/017
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
              of the M2-brane to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+superstring"} Green-Schwarz superstring
              was observed in
            %ul
              %li#DuffHoweInamiStelle87
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"} Paul Howe
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      Superstrings in
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi D
                            %mo =
                            %mn 10
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=10
                      from Supermembranes in
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi D
                            %mo =
                            %mn 11
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11
                  %strong 191
                  (1987) 70 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(87)91323-2"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(87)91323-2
                  ]
                %p
                  also in:
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"} Michael Duff
                  (ed.):
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"} The World in Eleven Dimensions
                  205-206 (1987) [
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/245249"}> spire:245249
                  ]
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"}> Paul Townsend
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The eleven-dimensional supermembrane revisited
                  %strong 350
                  (1995) 184-187 [
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9501068"}> arXiv:hep-th/9501068
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(95)00397-4"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(95)00397-4
            %p
              around the time when
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
              became accepted due to
            %ul
              %li#Witten95
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+Theory+Dynamics+In+Various+Dimensions"} String Theory Dynamics In Various Dimensions
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9503124"}> arXiv:hep-th/9503124
                )
            %p On the early history of these developments:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+A.+Bergshoeff"}> Eric A. Bergshoeff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+K.+Townsend"} Paul K. Townsend
                %em A brief history of supermembranes
                [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.06234"}> arXiv:2503.06234
                ]
            %p See also:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                  %em SDiff Gauge Theory and the M2 Condensate
                  (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0808.1583"}> arXiv:0808.1583
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maria+P.+Garcia+del+Moral"}> Maria P. Garcia del Moral
                  , C. Las Heras, P. Leon, J. M. Pena,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alvaro+Restuccia"} Alvaro Restuccia
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      Fluxes, Twisted tori, Monodromy and
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
                      Supermembranes
                  %strong 2020
                  97 (2020) &amp;lbrack;
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.06397"}> arXiv:2005.06397
                  ,
                  = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP09(2020)097"} doi:10.1007/JHEP09(2020)097
            %p
              Discussion from the point of view of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} ∞-Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
            %ul
              %li#FSS2013
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
                (2013)
            %p
              On possible structures in M2-brane dynamics and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-M5-brane+bound+states"} M2-M5-brane bound states
              which could be
              = succeed "-lifts" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+system"} integrability
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+superstring"} Green-Schwarz superstring
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS+spacetime"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi AdS
                        %mn 5
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_5
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \times
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/5-sphere"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 5
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^5
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kirill+Gubarev"}> Kirill Gubarev
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edvard+Musaev"} Edvard Musaev
                %em Integrability structures in string theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.06486"}> arXiv:2301.06486
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#ReferencesForDBranes D-branes as GS-sigma models
          %p
            Green-Schwarz action functionals for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            (including the
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DBI+action"} DBI action
          %ul
            %li#CGNSW96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Cederwall"}> Martin Cederwall
                , Alexander von Gussich,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bengt+Nilsson"} Bengt Nilsson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Dirichlet Super-p-Branes in Ten-Dimensional Type IIA and IIB Supergravity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9611159"} arXiv:hep-th/9611159
            %li#APPS97b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mina+Aganagic"}> Mina Aganagic
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jaemo+Park"} Jaemo Park
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dual D-Brane Actions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9702133"} arXiv:hep-th/9702133
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#CAIB99"} CAIB 99
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Sakaguchi00"} Sakaguchi 00
          %h3#dualities Dualities
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            for the Green-Schwarz string is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mirjam+Cvetic"}> Mirjam Cvetic
                , H. Lu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Pope"} Christopher Pope
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
                = succeed "," do
                  %em T-Duality in the Green-Schwarz Formalism, and the Massless/Massive IIA Duality Map
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9907202"} arXiv:hep-th/9907202
            %li
              %p
                Bogdan Kulik, Radu Roiban,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em T-duality of the Green-Schwarz superstring
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0012010"} arXiv:hep-th/0012010
            %li#BandosJulia03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernard+Julia"} Bernard Julia
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superfield T-duality rules
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0303075"} arXiv:hep-th/0303075
              %p
                reviewed in
                %em Superfield T-duality rules in ten dimensions with one isometry
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0312299"}> arXiv:hep-th/0312299
                )
          %h3#ReferencesWZWTerm WZW terms, super Lie algebra cohomology and the brane scan
          %p
            The WZW nature of the second term in the GS action, recognized in (
            %a{:href => "#HenneauxMezincescu85"}> Henneaux-Mezincescu 85
            ) is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Rabin87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+Rabin"}> Jeffrey Rabin
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supermanifold Cohomology and the Wess-Zumino Term of the Covariant Superstring Action
                %strong 108
                (1987) 375-389 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104116532"}> euclid:cmp/1104116532
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                B. Milewski,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superstrings from sigma models
            %li
              %p
                A.P. Isaev, E.A. Ivanov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Sigma Model Formulation of Green-Schwarz Superstring
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/266793"} spire:266793
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.worldscientific.com/doi/abs/10.1142/S0217732389000423"} doi:10.1142/S0217732389000423
            %li#AzcarragaTownsend89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"}> José de Azcárraga
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superspace geometry and the classification of supersymmetric extended objects
                %strong 62
                22 (1989) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.62.2579"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.62.2579
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/284635"} spire:284635
          %p
            and with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+theory"} Lie theoretic
            meaning made fully explicit (in “FDA” language) in
          %ul
            %li#AzcarragaIzquierdo95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"}> José de Azcárraga
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Izquierdo"} José Izquierdo
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+Groups%2C+Lie+Algebras%2C+Cohomology+and+Some+Applications+in+Physics"} Lie Groups, Lie Algebras, Cohomology and Some Applications in Physics
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511599897"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511599897
          %p The original “brane scan” classification of GS action functionals by WZW terms:
          %ul
            %li#AETW87
              Anna Achúcarro,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Evans"} Jonathan Evans
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Wiltshire"} David Wiltshire
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Super
                  = succeed "-Branes" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %strong 198
              (1987) 441 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/22286"}> spire:22286
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(87)90896-3"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(87)90896-3
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://ir.canterbury.ac.nz/xmlui/bitstream/handle/10092/9041/12616571_pbrane.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/SuperpBranes.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A complete rigorous classification of all the relevant cocycles on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
            was given in
          %ul
            %li#Brandt12-13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Friedemann+Brandt"}> Friedemann Brandt
                ,
                %em Supersymmetry algebra cohomology
              %p
                %em I: Definition and general structure
                J. Math. Phys.51:122302, 2010, (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.2118"}> arXiv:0911.2118
                )
              %p
                %em> II: Primitive elements in 2 and 3 dimensions
                , J. Math. Phys. 51 (2010) 112303 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1004.2978"}> arXiv:1004.2978
                )
              %p
                %em> III: Primitive elements in four and five dimensions
                , J. Math. Phys. 52:052301, 2011 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1005.2102"}> arXiv:1005.2102
                )
              %p
                %em>
                  IV: Primitive elements in all dimensions from
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=4
                  to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 11
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11
                , J. Math. Phys. 54, 052302 (2013) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1303.6211"}> arXiv:1303.6211
                )
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 11
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 11
            the relevant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} cocycles
            have also been discussed (but not related to the Green-Schwarz action functional) in
          %ul
            %li#DAuriaFre82
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+D%27Auria"}> Riccardo D'Auria
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GeometricSupergravity.pdf", :title => "Geometric Supergravity in D=11 and its hidden supergroup"} Geometric Supergravity in D=11 and its hidden supergroup
          %p A review is in
          %ul
            %li#Duff87
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Supermembranes: the first fifteen weeks
              %strong 5
              (1988) 189 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/0264-9381/5/1/023"}> doi:10.1088/0264-9381/5/1/023
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/record/248034"} spire:248034
          %p from which the above table is taken.
          %p
            Systematic review and discussion of the 3- and 4-cocycles in the old
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            via the relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+algebras+and+supersymmetry"} division algebras and supersymmetry
            is in
          %ul
            %li#BaezHuerta10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Huerta"} John Huerta
              = succeed "," do
                %em Division algebras and supersymmetry II
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1003.3436"} arXiv:1003.34360
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              I. Bars, C. Deliduman and D. Minic, Phys. Rev D59 (1999) 125004; Phys. Lett. B457 (1999) 275. (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9812161"}> arXiv:hep-th/9812161
              )
          %p More along these lines is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
              , S. Ferrara,
              %em Four curious supergravities
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1010.3173"}> arXiv
              )
          %p
            The Green-Schwarz-type action for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            was found in
          %ul
            %li#BLNPST97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
                , Kurt Lechner, Alexei Nurmagambetov, Paolo Pasti,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Sorokin"} Dmitri Sorokin
                %em Covariant Action for the Super-Five-Brane of M-Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9701149"}> arXiv:hep-th/9701149
                )
            %li#APPS97
              %p
                Mina Aganagic, Jaemo Park, Costin Popescu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
                %em World-Volume Action of the M Theory Five-Brane
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9701166"}> arXiv:hep-th/9701166
                )
          %p
            The 7-cocycle on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
            which gives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+6-algebra"} supergravity Lie 6-algebra
            appears in these articles (somewhat secretly) in equation (
            %a{:href => "#BLNPST97"}> BLNPST, equation (9)
            ).
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#BPST
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
              , Paolo Pasti,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Sorokin"} Dmitri Sorokin
              %em Superbrane Actions and Geometrical Approach
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9705064"}> arXiv:hep-th/9705064
              )
          %p
            The 7-cocycle for the M5-brane on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+Lie+3-algebra"} supergravity Lie 3-algebra
            is equation (8.8) there.
          %p
            The interpretation of the cocycles for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            and for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            as cocycles on “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super-Minkowski+spacetime"}> extended super-Minkowski spacetime
            ” is due to
          %ul
            %li#CAIB99
              %p
                C. Chrysso‌malakos,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"} José de Azcárraga
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+M.+Izquierdo"} José M. Izquierdo
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The geometry of branes and extended superspaces
                %strong 567
                (2000) 293-330 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9904137"}> arXiv:hep-th/9904137
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0550-3213(99)00512-X"} doi:10.1016/S0550-3213(99)00512-X
            %li#Sakaguchi00
              %p
                Makoto Sakaguchi:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em IIB-Branes and New Spacetime Superalgebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9909143"} arXiv:hep-th/9909143
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/1126-6708/2000/04/019"} doi:10.1088/1126-6708/2000/04/019
            %li#AzcarragaIzquierdo01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"}> José de Azcárraga
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Izquierdo"} J. M. Izquierdo
                %em Superalgebra cohomology, the geometry of extended superspaces and superbranes
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0105125"}> arXiv:hep-th/0105125
                )
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+algebras+and+supersymmetry"} division algebras and supersymmetry
          %p
            A corresponding refinement of the brane scan to a “brane bouquet” of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} super L-∞ algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebra+cohomology"} extensions
            (hence in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+theory"} infinity-Lie theory
            via
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} ∞-Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
          %ul
            %li#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
                = succeed ":02" do
                  %strong 12
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.5264"} arXiv:1308.5264
            %li#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+WZW+term+of+the+M5-brane+and+differential+cohomotopy"} The WZW term of the M5-brane and differential cohomotopy
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1506.07557"} arXiv:1506.07557
            %li#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Rational+sphere+valued+supercocycles+in+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} Rational sphere valued supercocycles in M-theory and type IIA string theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1606.03206"}> arXiv:1606.03206
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vincent+Braunack-Mayer"}> Vincent Braunack-Mayer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Gauge+enhancement+of+Super+M-Branes"} Gauge enhancement of Super M-Branes
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.01115"}> arXiv:1806.01115
                )
          %p
            These cohomological arguments also appear in what is called the “ectoplasm” method for invariants in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
            in
          %ul
            %li#BossardHoweStelle09
              %p
                G. Bossard,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"} Paul Howe
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A note on the UV behaviour of maximally supersymmetric Yang-Mills theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0908.3883"} arXiv:0908.3883
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"}> Paul Howe
                , T. G. Pugh, K. S. Stelle, C. Strickland-Constable,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Ectoplasm with an Edge
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1104.4387"} arXiv:1104.4387
            %li
              %p
                G. Bossard,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"} Paul Howe
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulf+Lindstr%C3%B6m"} Ulf Lindström
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
                %em Integral invariants in maximally supersymmetric Yang-Mills theories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1012.3142"}> arXiv:1012.3142
                )
          %p The connection is made in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"}> Paul Howe
              , O. Raetzel,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
              = succeed "," do
                %em On Brane Actions and Superembeddings
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9804051"} arXiv:hep-th/9804051
          %p
            The other brane scan, listing consistent asymptotic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetimes"} spacetimes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superconformal+algebras"} superconformal algebras
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li#BlencoweDuff88
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miles+P.+Blencowe"}> Miles P. Blencowe
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"} Mike Duff
              = succeed "," do
                %em Supersingletons
              %strong 203
              3(1988) 229-236 (
              %a{:href => "http://cds.cern.ch/record/184143"}> cds:184143
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(88)90544-8"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(88)90544-8
          %p with further developments discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Duff09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Near-horizon brane-scan revived
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0804.3675"} arXiv:0804.3675
            %li#Duff21
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
                ,
                %em The conformal brane-scan: an update
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.13784"}> arXiv:2112.13784
                )
          %h3#ReferencesAdSBackgrounds Anti de Sitter backgrounds
          %p
            Discussion of Green-Schwarz strings on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+anti+de+Sitter+spacetimes"} super anti de Sitter spacetimes
            includes the following.
          %p General:
          %ul
            %li#HatsudaSakaguchi02
              %p
                Machiko Hatsuda, Makoto Sakaguchi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Wess-Zumino term for AdS superstring
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0205092"} arXiv:hep-th/0205092
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.66.045020"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.66.045020
            %li#HatsudaSakaguchi01
              %p
                Machiko Hatsuda, Makoto Sakaguchi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Wess-Zumino term for the AdS superstring and generalized Inonu-Wigner contraction
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0106114"} arXiv:hep-th/0106114
          %h4#ReferencesAdS5Background
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_5
          %p
            The super 3-cocycle for the Green-Schwarz
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} super anti de Sitter spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mn 5
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_5 \times S^5
            (i.e. on
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 5
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
