          %h3#ReferencesConservedCurrentAlgebra Conserved current algebra
          %p
            That higher WZW functionals and hence Green-Schwarz super
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+current"} conserved current
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+charge"} BPS charge
            algebras which are
            %a{:href => "super+Poincare+Lie+algebra#PolyvectorExtensions"} polyvector extensions
            of the supersymmetry algebras was observed in
          %ul
            %li#AGIT89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"}> José de Azcárraga
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jerome+Gauntlett"} Jerome Gauntlett
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Izquierdo"} J.M. Izquierdo
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological extensions of the supersymmetry algebra for extended objects
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/26393?ln=en"} spire
          %p reviewed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+de+Azc%C3%A1rraga"}> José de Azcárraga
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+M.+Izquierdo"} José M. Izquierdo
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+Groups%2C+Lie+Algebras%2C+Cohomology+and+Some+Applications+in+Physics"} Lie Groups, Lie Algebras, Cohomology and Some Applications in Physics
              , Cambridge monographs of mathematical physics, (1995)
          %p
            and generalized to super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+n-algebras"} Lie n-algebras
            of BPS charges in
          %ul
            %li#SatiSchreiber15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Lie+n-algebras+of+BPS+charges"} Lie n-algebras of BPS charges
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1507.08692"}> arXiv:1507.08692
              )
          %p
            This is for branes in the old
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strings"}> strings
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membranes"} membranes
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-branes"} NS5-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
          %p
            The generalization oft this perspective to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#SorokinTownsend97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Sorokin"}> Dmitri Sorokin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %em M-theory superalgebra from the M-5-brane
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9708003"} arXiv:hep-th/9708003
          %p
